<%# Student Portal > Pets (routes/student-portal.js, utils/pets.js) - the
    pet illustrations themselves, kept separate from partials/icon-sprite
    (that one's plain line icons for chrome/nav; these are small flat-
    color creature illustrations meant to be composited together).
    Every body symbol shares the same 0 0 120 120 canvas with the head
    centered around (60, 46) so the eyes/mouth/accessory overlay symbols
    line up on top of any species without per-species positioning -
    views/student-pets.ejs stacks body + eyes + mouth + accessory as
    sibling <use> elements inside one <svg>. Body shapes use
    fill="currentColor" for their main coat/shell/scale color so
    utils/pets.js's per-species color options work by just setting the
    wrapping element's CSS `color`; a few fixed-color accent shapes
    (belly patches, cheeks) stay literal hex since those don't change
    with the coat color trait. %>
